course: dictionary
lesson: 7219
title: Phonics: sounds and letters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Phonics is a way of learning to read by matching letters, and groups of letters, to the sounds they make. Sound it out: «sh» says /sh/, and «igh» says /eye/.
explain: Readers use phonics to blend sounds into a word: c-a-t, so cat. Spellers do the reverse. They split a word into its sounds to spell it, which is called segmenting.
explain: Phonics also means the lessons and books that teach this. Read the sentence around the word to see which meaning fits, the skill or the lessons.
fact: Phonics is a way of learning to read by matching letters to sounds.
fact: «Sh» says /sh/, and «igh» says /eye/.
fact: To blend means to put the sounds together to read a word: c-a-t, cat.
fact: To segment means to split a word into its sounds to spell it.
fact: «Phonics» can also mean the lessons and books that teach reading through sounds.
exercise: «Fluent readers still use phonics, fast and silently, and slow down to it when they meet a hard new word.» What does phonics mean here? | Reading a book with the lights off | *Matching letters to the sounds they make | A kind of pen used in schools | Learning to draw pictures
exercise: In phonics, what sound does «sh» make? | /oo/ | /ee/ | */sh/ | /k/
exercise: Ella reads c-a-t and says «cat». What is she doing? | *Blending the sounds together to read the word | Segmenting the word to spell it | Counting the letters | Drawing a picture of a cat
test: In the UK, when is the phonics screening check given? | Reception | Year 6 | *Year 1 | Year 9
test: What does the phrase «sound it out» mean? | Write the word in capital letters | Skip the word and never come back to it | Ask a friend to spell the word for you | *Say the sounds of the letters to read the word
exam: Which meaning fits «Our phonics lesson is on Monday»? | A kind of cake | A small animal that lives in the sea | Running fast in a race | *The lessons that teach reading through sounds
